This is Hidden Brain. I'm Shankar Vedantam. In his great novel, Anna Karenina, Leo Tolstoy spends hundreds of pages describing Count Vronsky's desperate longing to be with Anna, the woman he loves. He risks his reputation, his military career, his standing in society. He endures uncertainty, jealousy, torment. And finally, after all the struggle and sacrifice, he gets what he wants. Anna is his. But almost immediately, something strange happens.
这里是《隐藏的大脑》。我是尚卡尔·韦丹塔姆。在列夫·托尔斯泰的伟大小说《安娜·卡列尼娜》中，他花了几百页的篇幅来描写渥伦斯基伯爵对与他所爱的女人安娜在一起的绝望渴望。他冒着毁掉声誉、军事生涯和在社会上地位的风险。他忍受着不确定性、嫉妒和折磨。最后，经过所有的挣扎和牺牲，他得到了他想要的东西。安娜属于他了。但几乎就在同时，一件奇怪的事情发生了。

